delta-change "lexical-expressions"
message "LexicalExpressions first-class lexical expressions and token captures over GraphLexer"
author "ai"
doc "guide" """
  |# LexicalExpressions: first-class lexical expressions
  |
  |LexicalExpressions is the fifth post-constitution grammar product. It is **not** a new
  |foundation. The frozen constitutional staircase remains F0 through F11.
  |
  |LexicalExpressions is derived canonically from GraphLexer:
  |
  |```text
  |GraphLexer + LexicalExpressions.delta = LexicalExpressions
  |```
  |
  |Frozen identities:
  |
  |```text
  |LexicalExpressions.delta
  |c27fbb314a482a71226bde3a249c2212be7ee6d26f4ee87e6ba9f1216b9975eb
  |
  |LexicalExpressions root
  |3bfb6533b24369b04af9a0114355bd5805ab2fa987d410034f922e9a093fa4a3
  |```
  |
  |The resulting graph contains 444 nodes, 561 edges, and 444 entities.
  |
  |## Purpose
  |
  |GraphLexer made tokenization graph-selected, but its token vocabulary was still
  |limited to fixed grammar literals. LexicalExpressions makes dynamic lexical recognition a
  |first-class Trellis language rather than placing regular expressions in node
  |attributes or hard-coding one scanner per object language.
  |
  |The lexical expression vocabulary is:
  |
  |```text
  |lexer.literal
  |lexer.char-class
  |lexer.sequence
  |lexer.choice
  |lexer.repeat
  |```
  |
  |Named `lexer.rule` nodes bind those expressions to a lexical sort and a lexical
  |constructor. The LexicalExpressions interpreter is generic over this graph.
  |
  |## Bool0 lexical rules
  |
  |The example language now obtains three dynamic token classes entirely from
  |Trellis data.
  |
  |### Identifier
  |
  |```text
  |identifier-start
  |(identifier-rest)*
  |```
  |
  |`identifier-start` and `identifier-rest` are first-class character-class nodes.
  |Their host primitives are explicitly named Unicode operations, not embedded
  |regular expressions.
  |
  |### Number
  |
  |```text
  |digit+
  |```
  |
  |The digit class is the graph-selected `unicode-digit` primitive.
  |
  |### String
  |
  |```text
  |'"'
  |(
  |    string-unescaped
  |  | '\\' escape-code
  |)*
  |'"'
  |```
  |
  |The accepted escape codes are `"`, `\\`, `n`, `t`, and `r`. LexicalExpressions preserves
  |the lexical spelling as its AST lexeme; semantic escape decoding can therefore
  |be layered independently rather than being hidden inside the lexer.
  |
  |## Grammar token capture
  |
  |LexicalExpressions adds `grammar.token`. A token capture points to a first-class lexical
  |rule. The rule provides the lexical sort and leaf constructor, so a grammar
  |production does not duplicate either type.
  |
  |The example adds:
  |
  |```text
  |Var       : Name   -> Expr
  |NumberLit : Number -> Expr
  |StringLit : String -> Expr
  |```
  |
  |Their values are represented at runtime as `FieldValue.Lexeme`. Existing
  |TemplateGrammar through GraphLexer trees remain byte-for-byte product identities and
  |keep their previous `Tree` shape.
  |
  |## Deterministic token selection
  |
  |LexicalExpressions retains longest-match selection. Equal-length candidates are resolved
  |by graph-defined priority and then stable lexical identity:
  |
  |```text
  |longest-match
  |priority-then-lexical
  |```
  |
  |Fixed grammar literals have priority 0. Dynamic rules have explicit positive
  |priorities. Consequently `true` remains the Bool0 keyword while `truex` is an
  |identifier, with no keyword table in Scala.
  |
  |## Semantic evolution
  |
  |The free `DeltaBool0` language admits lexical expression nodes. For example,
  |changing the graph-resident identifier-start primitive to `unicode-digit`
  |changes recognition so that `1abc` becomes one identifier, without changing
  |scanner code.
  |
  |An attempt to inject a payload such as `regex:[A-Za-z_]` is rejected because it
  |is not a member of the graph-defined primitive character-class vocabulary.
  |LexicalExpressions therefore removes a common route by which a second hidden language
  |could leak back into node attributes.
  |
  |## Compatibility
  |
  |`Language.graph-lexer` remains the frozen GraphLexer product graph.
  |`Language.graph` advances to LexicalExpressions. The test suite checks observational
  |parity on the GraphLexer surface before exercising LexicalExpressions-only token classes.
  |
  |The F0 through F11 Scala/Rust clean-room parity harness is unchanged and must
  |remain green.
  |
  """
test "canonical delta contract"
  assert "canonical"
  assert "valid"
  assert "source-roundtrip"
  assert "dependency" "graph-lexer"
  assert "introduces" "grammar.component.token" "grammar.component"
